  "lemmas": [
    {
      "id": "Lemma 1",
      "statement": "v is forceable iff delta_v (x) tau lies in W|_U, the restriction of the module's row space to the unforced coordinates",
      "status": "proved; both engines agree on 300 random instances"
    },
    {
      "id": "P1",
      "statement": "a generator at a vertex already in T is useless",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "statement": "two non-parallel generators at a vertex force it; a third or a parallel duplicate adds nothing",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "statement": "dim W >= n - |T|, hence m + r >= n - |T| and score >= 1",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "statement": "every vertex outside T must see two non-parallel directions among its incident edge labels and its own generators",
      "status": "proved; pins mandatory generator positions"
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "statement": "two non-parallel generators at v contribute exactly delta_v (x) Q^2 regardless of which pair",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "statement": "in any object with score < 2 every vertex carries at most one generator, and r <= n (T strictly beats a double generator)",
      "status": "proved; 419 random instances checked; 6x search speedup"
    },
    {
      "id": "P7/P8",
      "statement": "cut lemma: Sigma_A(f) lies in span(labels crossing the cut) + span(generator labels inside A). A={v} gives P4; A=V with T empty gives: tau must be in the span of the generator labels alone, so r>=2 with two distinct slopes, and a generator-free object with T empty forces nothing",
      "status": "proved; 515 instances checked; exhaustive r=0 sweeps over 5 boxes all empty"
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "statement": "nested-cut chain: every A_j = {v_j..v_q} in the forcing order must be crossed with rank 2, i.e. the object admits a rank-2 elimination ordering",
      "status": "proved; not yet used as a prune"
    },
    {
      "id": "Theorem 2",
      "statement": "if at most two distinct slopes are used then the score is >= 2",
      "status": "proved; 445 instances checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "Chain remark",
      "statement": "gluing D copies of a block with per-gap interfaces is score-neutral when copies are forced one at a time; improvements need interleaved forcing orders",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "id": "one-level scheme formula",
      "statement": "g(beta) = (e + w + u(beta-1)/beta)/c with fixed point c*beta^2 - (e+u+w)*beta + u = 0; reproduces KT Cor 3.5, and shows the naive one-level corner scheme lands below 3/2 hence is unrealisable",
      "status": "derived; 199 integer skeletons land in (3/2, 1.675]"
    }
  ],
  "key_findings": [
    "gamma is a LIMIT of the corner ladder, attained by no finite object; the Epoch target 1.675 sits 1.309e-4 BELOW gamma, so the task requires a construction outside the published family",
    "our 7/4 object matches Epoch's own Figure 3 vertex for vertex, and our engine forces the same vertex first as their hand derivation; same for their Figure 2 (11/6)",
    "the search independently rediscovers min|R| = 4 for the published 11/6 shape and the 7/4 trapezoid from bare box dimensions",
    "exhaustive n=4: best score 7/4 over four slopes with |T|=0 and over six slopes with |T|<=1",
    "first denominator q = n-|T| at which 1.675 is exactly reachable is q = 40; every smaller q that beats the record must reach <= 5/3",
    "Goal 2 (beat 11/6 with three slopes) is the softer prize; its gentlest targets are q = 10, 11, 12"
  ],
